## What this lane was

The pinned Smithsonian USNM 15259 cranium/mandible GLBs render as bounding
boxes in `tools/science_funnel/validation/visual_proof_20260917/` because
their geometry decode was REFUSED: they are Draco-compressed
(KHR_draco_mesh_compression, edgebreaker method 1 / valence traversal type 2,
bitstream 2.2) and a pure-Python port was falsified. The operator-delegated
decision: decode via the OFFICIAL Google Draco WASM decoder in a browser
page. This lane executed that decision.

## What was done (in order)

1. RULE 0 FIRST — `work.data.visual_proof_20260917` revision 3 banked BEFORE
   any code (tools/creature_graph/validation/admit_visual_proof_20260917.py,
   idempotent + revision-aware; revision 2 superseded). Two more falsified
   premises banked: (d) all Smithsonian plain-named derivatives are ALSO
   draco (cran/mand medium+low probed); (e) no Python Draco decoder on PyPI
   (pydraco/pydraco3/draco-loader 404). Falsifier stated pre-run.
2. Browser decode channel (all mechanics PowerShell; harness in
   tools/science_funnel/validation/draco_decode_20260918/):
   - serve_draco.ps1 — raw TcpListener HTTP server on 127.0.0.1:8791
     (NOT 8127), serves harness + pinned cdn/ libs + the two GLBs + POST
     back-channel for results.
   - harness.html — three.js r160 (GLTFLoader+DRACOLoader, import map) over
     the OFFICIAL gstatic draco_wasm_wrapper.js + draco_decoder.wasm 1.5.7.
     Pure-JS sha256 (self-tested against the "abc" vector in-page), decodes
     each GLB TWICE with FRESH DRACOLoader/WASM instances, extracts
     positions/normals/indices as typed arrays, hashes bytes, captures a
     labelled PERCEPTUAL EVIDENCE screenshot (WebGL, software rasterizer),
     and POSTs buffers + hashes back. Corrupt probe: flips ONE byte inside
     the draco bufferView (offset recorded) and attempts decode.
   - run_decode.ps1 / compare_decode_runs.ps1 — orchestration, two full page
     runs (run1, run2), cross-run comparison, decode_receipt.json.
   - install_decode_artifacts.ps1 — pins decoded buffers + screenshots into
     the repo and re-verifies the chain on disk.
   - CDN pins (fetched sha256s in cdn.lock.json, bytes committed in cdn/):
     three.module.js 76dea815..., GLTFLoader.js d073b438..., DRACOLoader.js
     65c114ec..., BufferGeometryUtils.js 9be041e9..., draco_wasm_wrapper.js
     e8049906..., draco_decoder.wasm 2516a4e4...
3. FALSIFIERS — ALL HELD:
   - decode determinism: position/normal/index buffer sha256s identical
     across fresh-decoder in-run passes AND two separate page runs.
     cranium pos 3d48583302999116... (133,172 verts, 449,997 indices);
     mandible pos e73d24836219fee7... (97,967 verts, 449,997 indices).
   - corrupted GLB: one flipped byte inside the draco bufferView -> decode
     REFUSED loudly in both runs (GLTFLoader throws; recorded verbatim).
   - renderer: refuses loudly on any pinned-buffer hash mismatch; foreign
     GLB bytes (sha not matching the decode record) fall back to the honest
     bbox+refusal render — never fake geometry.
4. Renderer wiring — tools/science_funnel/visual_proof.py:
   - load_decode_identity() gates on glb sha256 + ALL buffer file sha256s
     before any geometry render; render_glb_geometry() = software z-buffer,
     two-sided Lambert, document.json camera; labelled with the position
